nissa's source rules: a directory is entered from outside only through its interfaces.ts (tests may also use its testing.ts), production never imports a test-side file, an interfaces.ts defines what it offers rather than forwarding it, and no source file is longer than 1,750 lines. Here harness/lib/ is one directory, entered from outside through harness/lib/interfaces.ts; harness/lib/reach/, harness/lib/cut/ and harness/lib/shapes/ are directories of their own, each entered through its interfaces.ts; and harness/lib/reach/testing/fixtures/ stands for code outside the harness, vendored on purpose. This repository lands by pushing to GitHub's main, and git-hooks' astra-source-rules-push judges each such push made from the house with source-tooling's `js source-rules`, its new tip against main's old, refusing one that raises any rule's measure. `js source-rules --root .` lists what stands, and AGENTS.md names the three floors it counts.
